# DRAM geometry for AML-S905X-CC (Le Potato), GXL + DDR3, 32-bit bus.
#
# Stack it on the shipping open-chain defconfig:
#
#   make libretech-cc_libre_defconfig dram-libretech-cc.config olddefconfig
#
# That is the stack LBS names in configs/aml-s905x-cc-libre-2rank, and it is
# the only one this fragment has that builds: measured 2026-08-30 at
# v2026.07/lc-master e8fba1cfb00, SPL 38115 B of the 45056 B (0xb000) amlimage
# ceiling, gate OK.
#
# The recipe printed here until 2026-08-30 --
#
#   make libretech-cc_defconfig spl-usb.config dram-libretech-cc.config \
#        olddefconfig
#
# -- does NOT link at that tip: 0xb2f3 B against the 0xb000 ceiling, "excess:
# 0x2f3 bytes".  configs/spl-usb.config is composition notes only and carries
# the measurement; do not revive that stack to build this fragment.
#
# Why this file exists.  libretech-cc_defconfig sets no CONFIG_DRAM_* at all --
# it builds no SPL, so the symbols are not even visible in it (they live behind
# `if MESON_GX && SPL`).  configs/spl-usb.config is shared with the DDR4
# AML-S905X-CC-V2 and so cannot carry a per-part geometry either.  With nothing
# stating the rank count, the Kconfig choice fell through to its first entry and
# a 2 GB two-rank board was built as one rank.  Read back off the live DMC on
# 2026-08-08 as DMC_DDR_CTRL=0x00200064.
#
# Omitting this fragment is no longer a correctness bug -- the map is the same
# for one rank and two, and dram_init() narrows the DMC range decode to the
# detected size -- but it costs the upper rank, i.e. half the RAM.
#
# The 2 GB SKU is two 1 GB ranks, two Nanya NT5CB256M16DP-EK per rank (4 Gbit
# 256M x16, 15 row / 10 column / 3 bank bits, 2 KB page), from the production
# BOM and schematic; vendor BL2 reports "Rank0: 1024MB / Rank1: 1024MB" on this
# board.
#
# The 1 GB SKU's construction is NOT established.  If it is the same device
# depopulated to one rank, CONFIG_DRAM_ONE_RANK=y here is all it needs -- the
# geometry, and so the address map, is identical.  If instead it is four 2 Gbit
# x16 devices as two 512 MB ranks, it has 14 row bits and needs its OWN map;
# this fragment does not serve it and neither does the map in dram-gx.c.  One
# line of a vendor-BL2 boot log on a 1 GB board settles it: "1 rank x 1024MB"
# against "2 ranks x 512MB".  Do not guess it from this file.
#
# Selecting two ranks on a one-rank board is not fatal -- detection finds
# 1024 MB and reports it -- but the PHY spends training time on a rank that is
# not fitted.
#
# The BOM specs the DRAM generically with an empty alternates column, and
# amlogic/gxl/s905x/ddr/"DDR Test Results.docx" records a UNIIC-populated board
# labelled 1.35 V crashing at 912 MHz.  The Nanya part is the reference fit,
# not a guarantee that every board carries it.
CONFIG_DRAM_DDR3=y
CONFIG_DRAM_TWO_IDENTICAL_RANKS=y

# 912 MHz is the vendor's figure for this board, not a JEDEC bin, and the part
# number is not established.  2T is the vendor command rate.
CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=912
CONFIG_DRAM_2T_MODE=y

# CONFIG_DRAM_DQS_CORR is NOT set here because it is not this file's to set.
# The DDR3 open chain enables it in configs/libretech-cc_libre_defconfig, which
# is the one config aml-s905x-cc-libre names; a target is ONE defconfig and this
# fragment is not in that target's stack, so a line here would enable nothing on
# the shipping path.  This file is an instrument-bench leftover, kept only for
# the aml-s905x-cc-libre-eye* arms.
#
# The objection that used to stand here is retracted, and its wording must not
# be re-quoted.  It read that the correction "rewrites trained delay values by
# hard-coded 95/100 and 88/100 factors with branches that write literal zero".
# The factors are real and are Le Potato's OWN vendor values (boot-lite
# board/aml-s905x-cc/firmware/timing.c, non-LPDDR3 arm: wr {100,100,95,95,95,95}
# / rd {100,100,88,95,95,100}, byte-for-byte the #else arm of
# dram-settings-gx.h that a DDR3 board compiles).  The literal-zero branches are
# NOT: they belonged to the prior DQSCORR_DX macro, which dram-gxl.c records as
# replaced and which has no caller on this branch.  The live code does the
# OPPOSITE -- a zero GUARD, `if (!v) v = 1`, at each of the three scaling sites
# in meson_dram_phy_setup_ranks(), so a trained zero is floored to one rather
# than written back as zero.
#
# The remaining clause -- that every open-path measurement so far ran with it
# off -- is true, and it conditions that corpus rather than arguing against the
# setting: it describes what has been measured, not what the vendor does.
# Position, evidence and the boot gate:
# amlogic/software/boot/gxl/dram/design/dqs-corr-enable-decision.md.
